==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Dishwasher open for loading.jpg|thumb|'''Dishwasher''', open and loaded with dishes.]]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|dish|washer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈdɪʃˌwɒʃə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈdɪʃˌwɑʃɚ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|Dishwasher US.ogg|Audio (U.S.A.)|lang=en}}
* {{audio|EN-AU ck1 dishwasher.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[machine]] for washing dishes.
# Someone who washes dishes, especially one [[hired]] to wash dishes in a [[restaurant]].
# {{lb|en|UK|dialect|Wiltshire}} A [[European]] [[bird]], the [[wagtail]].
# {{lb|en|AU}} A bird, the [[restless flycatcher]] (''Myiagra inquieta'').

